a refusal requires its exit status and causal diagnostic: true
the same diagnostic at status 0 is not a refusal: true
status 1 with another diagnostic is not the expected refusal: true
diagnostics cannot match through the wrong stream: true
a causal diagnostic cannot be assembled across output streams: true
complete diagnostic fragments may come from either captured stream: true
large streams stay separate and do not fill an unread pipe: true
capture files are removed after normal and faulted child statuses: true
a relative executable still runs from another directory: true
the parent directory is restored after a successful spawn: true
spawn failure restores the parent directory: true
spawn failure removes both capture files: true
a bad child directory preserves the parent directory: true
a bad child directory removes both capture files: true
echoed child Verdict markers cannot become a parent's line-initial report: true
no echoed child marker starts a parent log line: true
diagnostic reporting also leaves no capture files: true
